SUMMARY:AYPROS X GREENWORKS: French Broad RIVER CLEANUP
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Young Professionals (AYPROS)\n*YOU MUST REGISTER WIT
 H GREENWORKS [HERE](https://dash.pointapp.org/events/743945?token=3bbe6cf4
 -4d13-428f-83d7-e3037e781022) OR IN THE LINK BELOW.*\n\nMake a visible dif
 ference on the French Broad River while spending the day alongside other y
 oung professionals who care about Asheville and Western North Carolina.\n\
 nAYPROS is sponsoring a hands-on river cleanup with Asheville GreenWorks o
 n Saturday\, August 1. Volunteers will paddle canoes\, with some participa
 nts potentially using kayaks\, along a section of the French Broad River. 
 We will stop frequently to remove litter from the water\, riverbanks\, and
  surrounding muddy areas.\n\nThis is not a simple walk along the shoreline
 . Volunteers should expect to enter water that may reach or rise above the
 ir waists\, move through muddy spaces\, and get dirty. It will be challeng
 ing\, rewarding\, and a chance to make a real contribution to the health o
 f one of our region’s most important natural resources.\n\nPlastic and o
 ther litter left in the river can travel far beyond Asheville and eventual
 ly reach the ocean. Every bag removed helps protect wildlife\, improve the
  health of our waterways\, and reduce the amount of plastic moving downstr
 eam.\n\nNew and longtime AYPROS members are welcome. You do not need to al
 ready know anyone in the group. Come ready to work\, meet other young prof
 essionals\, and spend a Saturday taking care of the place we call home.\n\
 n## Event Details\n\n**Saturday\, August 1\, 2026**\n**10:00 AM - 2:00 PM*
 *\n\n## Meeting Location\n\n**Silver-Line Park**\n1050 Riverside Drive\nWo
 odfin\, NC 28804\nThere is plenty of parking at Silver-Line Park. Voluntee
 rs are encouraged to park along the left side after entering the parking l
 ot.\nThe cleanup will end at the Asheville GreenWorks boatyard:\n\n**Ashev
 ille GreenWorks Boatyard**\n1444 Riverside Drive\nAsheville\, NC 28804\n\n
 **Asheville GreenWorks will coordinate the necessary vehicle shuttle to th
 e takeout location.** Volunteers should expect approximately one hour of p
 reparation\, instructions\, and shuttle coordination before getting onto t
 he river.\n\n## What Volunteers Will Do\n\n* Paddle a canoe or kayak along
  a section of the French Broad River\n* Stop regularly to remove litter fr
 om the river and surrounding areas\n* Walk through water that may reach ab
 ove the waist\n* Work in wet and muddy conditions\n* Help collect and remo
 ve trash from the waterway\n\n## What Asheville GreenWorks Will Provide\n\
 n* Boats\n* Paddles\n* Life jackets\n* Gloves\n* Trash bags\n* All other n
 ecessary cleanup equipment\n\n## What to Wear\n\nPlease dress for water\, 
 mud\, and physical activity:\n\n* Quick-dry or athletic T-shirt or long-sl
 eeve shirt\n* Quick-dry or athletic shorts\n* Swimsuit or synthetic underg
 arments beneath your clothing\n* An old pair of sneakers or secure river s
 hoes\n* Wool socks or another pair of thick socks\n* Hat or visor\n* Sungl
 asses\n\n**Do not wear cotton shorts. Flip-flops\, slides\, Crocs\, and ba
 re feet are not permitted during the cleanup.**\n\n## What to Bring\n\n* S
 unscreen\n* Towel\n* Complete change of clothes for the ride home\n\n## Re
 gistration Required\n\nRegistration must be completed directly through Ash
 eville GreenWorks. There are **24 spaces available for AYPROS volunteers**
 .\nWhen registering\, select the **AYP Volunteer** shift.\nThe separate **
 StreamKeeper** shift is reserved for volunteers who have already completed
  Asheville GreenWorks training.\n\n**[Register through Asheville GreenWork
 s](https://dash.pointapp.org/events/743945?token=3bbe6cf4-4d13-428f-83d7-e
 3037e781022)**\nRegistering through the Asheville GreenWorks link is requi
 red to participate. Space is limited\, so please reserve your place as soo
 n as possible.\n\n### Need Help Finding Us?\n\nIf you have trouble locatin
 g the group or are running a few minutes behind\, call or text AYPROS Crew
  Leader **Danielle Klein** at **239-287-8952**.\n\n## About AYPROS Leaders
 hip & Service\n\nAt AYPROS\, leadership is not only about titles. It is ab
 out stepping forward\, showing up\, and doing work that matters.\nOur Lead
 ership & Service events give young professionals the opportunity to work a
 longside local organizations addressing real needs across Asheville and We
 stern North Carolina. This cleanup is a chance to serve the community\, ca
 re for the French Broad River\, and get to know others who want to make As
 heville stronger.
